  "reason": "Evidence: All 6 completed experiments used multiprofile, and the best (config_032: scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted) reached 0.7250. The single-profile dimension is completely untested, creating significant uncertainty about whether multiprofile + transformer aggregation is truly superior or whether single profile with the same strong encoders could match or exceed it. This experiment (config_017: scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, singleprofile, weighted) directly tests that question using the best-known RNA and image encoders with the slightly better fusion strategy. It is the best use of experiment 7 because: (1) it resolves a major unexplored design axis before committing the remaining 3 experiments to refinement, (2) it leverages the strongest components already validated, and (3) if single profile performs comparably, it opens a new search space; if it underperforms, it confirms multiprofile is essential and we can focus remaining budget on fine-tuning the multiprofile configuration."
}

